# AGENT_MISSION

> Copy this file to `openspec/AGENT_MISSION.md` and customize it for your project.
> Remove this note when done.

This file enables a Claude Code agent to autonomously work through the roadmap in `openspec/ROADMAP.md`, one change at a time, without per-change user checkpoints.

## Working Directory

All commands run from: `<project-root>`

## Mode: Autonomous

Per-change CHECKPOINTs are **skipped**. The agent proceeds through the entire roadmap without pausing. A **mandatory stop** is produced at the end of the session.

## Flow per Change

For each change in `openspec/ROADMAP.md`, in order:

```bash
# 1. Create branch
git checkout -b feat/<change-name>

# 2. Create skeleton and artifacts
npx openspec new change "<change-name>"
# /opsx:new + /opsx:continue (loop until isComplete: true)
# OR: /opsx:propose <change-name> for a one-step fast-forward

# 3. Commit artifacts
git add openspec/ && git commit -m "docs(<change-name>): add proposal, design and tasks"

# 4. Implement (TDD — tests first)
# /opsx:apply — work through tasks one by one
# → commit each meaningful step

# 5. Verify
# /opsx:verify — fix all CRITICALs

# 6. AI Review
# Spawn laravel-simplifier agent — fix critical findings
# → commit: "refactor(<change-name>): apply review feedback"

# 7. Recap
# /recap — three-section explanation with Mermaid diagram

# 8. Refactor
# /simplify with these three questions:
#   - "What is the smallest safe change that makes this codebase better?"
#   - "Can a new developer follow the flow without mental jumps?"
#   - "Which refactoring steps preserve behavior but improve structure?"
# → commit if changes made: "refactor(<change-name>): <improvement>"

# 9. Sync + Archive
# /opsx:sync → git add openspec/ && git commit -m "docs(<change-name>): sync specs"
# /opsx:archive → git add openspec/ && git commit -m "docs(<change-name>): archive change"

# 10. PR + Merge
git rebase -i --autosquash origin/main
git push -u origin feat/<change-name>
gh pr create --title "feat(<change-name>): <description>"
gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch
git checkout main && git pull && git remote prune origin
```

## Rules

- All tests must pass before any commit (pre-commit hook enforces this)
- TDD: write the test first, then implement
- Keep each change focused — one concern, max 15 tasks
- Use `npx openspec` for all OpenSpec CLI calls (local dependency, not global)
- If a change is blocked or unclear, STOP and describe the blocker — do not guess

## Mandatory Stop

After completing all changes (or when blocked), produce this summary:

```
## Session Summary

| Change | Branch (deleted) | Commits | Tests |
|--------|-----------------|---------|-------|
| <name> | feat/<name>     | N       | N passed |

## Review
- All changes merged to main
- Run: php artisan test --compact
- Review: git log --oneline --graph main
- Open PRs: <url if any>
```

Then stop. Do not start another change unless explicitly asked.
